# Foundry
#
# `contracts/lib/` used to be ignored here, and that one line is why continuous
# integration was red. The workflow checks the repo out with `submodules:
# recursive` and runs `forge build`, but neither dependency was ever committed,
# so every run since the job was added has failed on a missing OpenZeppelin
# import. The README meanwhile claimed a passing test suite. Build artefacts
# are still ignored; the sources the build needs are not.
contracts/out/
contracts/out-recipientbound/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/
.env.local

# never commit any env variant, including backups
.env*
!.env.example

